      "heading": "B — Audience and scope",
      "learner_facing": false,
      "markdown": "## B — Audience and scope\n\nAudience: first-time Iowa license applicants learning what each assistance feature does, what it cannot do, and which ones test day allows, in plain English.\n\nPrerequisites: basic driving vocabulary is assumed; this section teaches technology literacy, not vehicle operation.\n\nScope note: warning, assist, and convenience technologies only. Occupant safety and impairment live in later sections.\n\nSorting emphasis: warn-only versus acting versus banned calls are practiced as classification decisions, so this section feeds the dedicated technology-sorting surface declared in part C.\n",
